## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run build
```

Open `<%= name %>.rbxl` in Roblox Studio and press Play. Commit `wally.lock`.
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>

This is a Hybrid project: Rojo syncs `src` and `Packages` with `rojo serve`, and your Studio place
owns the world.
<% } -%>

## Scripts

| Script | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | Builds `<%= name %>.rbxl` |
| `npm run format` | Formats `src` |
| `npm run check` | Formats, lints and type checks `src` |
| `npm run createAction`, `createTag`, `createResource`, `createController`, `createCommand`, `createHint`, `createDomain` | Creates a definition; see [Definition Generators](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/definition-generators) |

Numeric Property definitions live in `src/server/Properties`. Register custom IDs there before referencing them from Tags, Resources or Action cost multipliers. Resource generator flags accept a registered Property ID, for example `--max MaxMana`; defaults belong in the Property definition.
